module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_roster_sweep_counts_a_bound_or_label_spelling_as_an_unbound_call" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep emits an import for a row's home in a module where the row's spelling occurs only as a LEXICALLY BOUND reference (a fn parameter) or as an ARGUMENT LABEL, never as a free call to the ambient name. The generated import binds a name the module does not use and sits beside a same-spelled parameter, a shadowing a later resolve may refuse or, worse, silently prefer.",
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL wave 1, PR #14317, 2026-10-18): the home-restricted apply (roster_import_sweep_apply_home_exit home=std.host_text) wrote `import std.host_text { chars }` into test.claim.site_gunb_ai_layout_witness and test.claim.site_gunb_ai_tokens_witness. In both, `chars` is the parameter of `fn var_name_at(s: String, at: Int, limit: Int, chars: List<String>)`, read as `join(chars, \"\")`, and the argument label of the call `var_name_at(s: s, at: at + 6, limit: limit, chars: [])`. No free `chars` call exists in either file. The two edits were reverted by hand in #14317, and this row is the record of why; the defect itself is not repaired there.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: roster_needed_rows counts sites through roster_sites_count, which takes every ScopedReferenceSite whose head classification is HeadLexicallyUnbound and whose spelling is the row's call. The specimen shows that classification reports at least one of the two positions above as lexically unbound -- an argument label is not a reference at all, and a parameter reference is bound by its fn. Which of the two produced the count is NOT established here: the run reported only the resulting EDIT row, not the site that justified it.",
    "SECOND SPECIMEN, A MIS-EDIT (probe on #14338, 2026-10-18): `fn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int { chars(s: x) }` -- a parameter named chars that is itself CALLED -- received both `import std.host_text { chars }` and the relabel `chars(s: x)` -> `chars(text: x)`. The collector reported the parameter's call head as HeadLexicallyUnbound, so the import count and the label plan both took it for the free name; the rename rewrote a call to the parameter, not to the home. The defect is therefore not confined to an unused import.",
    "INTERIM GUARD (tidy-ant-251's ruling C): v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_name_locally_bound refuses home-name-locally-bound for any module that binds a row's call spelling (parameter, let, match binder, lambda parameter), read from the binders themselves; both specimens are enrolled controls that must refuse. The guard only refuses. Its dissolution trigger is this row's trigger. The front-end defect itself is dispatched separately as a chain re-derivation in v2.compiler.lexical_scope / reference_site_collector.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the generator's own output was inspected and the two edits reverted before commit; nothing mechanical exposed it. HARM if missed: an unused import shadowing a parameter in every module where an ambient name doubles as a local name, generated at sweep scale.",
        "REPAIRED AT THE SITE, FOR THE POSITION HALF (v2.compiler.reference_site_collector + v2.compiler.occurrence_role + v2.workflow.roster_home_kind, PR #14435, 2026-10-19/20): every recorded site now carries the POSITION it was reached at, issued by ONE producer (v2.compiler.occurrence_role reference_position_step, which consumes the core marker table and v2.compiler.lexical_scope arrow_slot), and v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_site_is_free asks v2.workflow.roster_home_kind roster_site_needs_home_import, THE ONE RULE: a site needs its home import only when its head is unbound AND its position is compatible with the KIND the home declaration declares (TypeAnnotation/Return <-> a TYPE declaration, Value <-> a VALUE declaration -- fn, service, or a typed `data` constant, per the host item_kind at v1_compiler_infer_items.rs:274 where DataItem requires a body -- Label/PatternTag <-> neither unless the declaration says so), the kind read from the home declaration identity by v2.std.decl_index decl_facts_at, never from the spelling -- no shape tests, no second decider. When the census itself cannot classify the home the rule must decide about -- no keyed row classifies the declaration, or every keyed row is OtherItem (the census's own cannot-classify answer) -- the verdict is KindUnclassified and the answer is NEITHER a silent import NOR a silent no-import: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_any_unclassified_head refuses the module with the typed, located reason home-kind-unclassified home=<home> name=<name>, outranking even Clean (review 83187; DESIGN 5). The unclassified-home trio (roster_kind_controls: unclassifiable-home-is-not-free, unclassified-home-refuses, classified-home-flips-to-row + classified-home-imports over the same head and position at a census-classified home) measures that the refusal fires exactly on the census's inability, never from the position alone. (An earlier revision of this receipt said roster_site_is_free `refuses any head whose position is not ValuePosition`; that was the position-only draft the roster correction of 2026-10-19 replaced, and review 83116 caught the sentence contradicting the code.) The specimen's signature spelling is therefore `label/unbound` and never counts as a free name, while the body call head is `value/frame`. Measured: the same run reports SPECIMEN=CLEAN for both files and CALLED=CLEAN. v2.compiler.module_acquisition reads the BINDING fact alone, so an imported or undecided head stays a non-candidate whatever its position.",
    "STILL OPEN AFTER THAT REPAIR, so this row does not close: the INTERIM GUARD above is now a second path beside the modeled one and retires in its own PR -- delete v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_name_locally_bound's two call sites (roster_rows_label_plan:816's locally-bound label refusal and roster_sweep_rows:964's RefusalHomeNameLocallyBound import-row refusal), proved by that fn's own three-shape controls plus this row's specimen controls coming back Clean and correctly relabelled with it removed. Two neighbouring defects are named follow-ups, not repaired here: signature mentions that never reach a value frame (a function's own return-type head at [u/] and a free call head at [u/AB/] read UNBOUND whether or not a parameter of that declaration is in scope -- frame threading, not position), and the sweep's import authority: site_head_is_undecided reads scope.imported, so the head answer depends on a CALLER-supplied list -- measured on one fixture, an imported head reads UNBOUND when the caller passes no rows and UNDECIDED when it passes them. All three production call sites do pass rows (v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_identity_checked, v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_label_plan and roster_needed_rows); the no-row readings are the two deliberate no-import fixtures in v2.test.claim.lexical_scope. So the classifier reads imports from a parameter rather than from the tree it is handed, and a caller that forgets the list silently gets free names for imported heads.",
    "GUARD DISSOLVED (Seat 13, tidy-ant-251 option (i)): the let-binder cell was the one thing the interim guard still covered. v2.compiler.lexical_scope child_is_declaring_occurrence now keeps a `let` binder's declaring occurrence out of v2.compiler.reference_site_collector's sites (its uses already read HeadBoundInFrame), so roster_name_locally_bound, RefusalHomeNameLocallyBound and LabelsLocallyBound are deleted and roster_control_free_call_beside_param / _let / _pun pair each binder form with a free call in a sibling fn. A match-arm record pun stays UNDECIDED by design (resolve decides it, not the collector) and is not counted; the pun control pins that. EXECUTED READING (sleek-owl-397, srv1): the let and pun controls hold; the PARAMETER cell does not yet: a parameter named like a row beside a free call elsewhere now refuses label-sites-ambiguous (the label plan's head count and the collector's free-site count disagree), where the guard refused home-name-locally-bound. Same loud outcome, different reason; roster_control_free_call_beside_param pins that refusal and the intended import for the free call is the parameter cell's remaining work, so this row stays open for it. Restoration of the guard is not needed; the capability named below is the collector's own binder honouring.",
"PARAMETER CELL (PR #14897). Root cause, chain-derived: v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_label_plan compared the parse tree's primary-expression heads spelled like the row (a bound bare `chars` in `h(s: chars)` included) with the collector's FREE-site count, so a bound mention was a head the free count omitted (2 vs 1). The repair: v2.compiler.reference_site_collector ScopedReferenceSite now carries the occurrence of the node it was read at, and roster_label_plan JOINS each parse head to the value-position site starting at the same source byte (identity, not order), relabelling only heads whose site is free and refusing label-sites-ambiguous for any head or site it cannot place. roster_control_free_call_beside_param now requires the import, beside free_call_after_param and nested_call_beside_param. EXECUTED READING (sleek-owl-397, srv1, head b78bdc5a): roster-import-sweep-controls exit=0, CONTROL-FAIL=0, no label-sites-ambiguous refusal, so span_index records extents for the normalized occurrence ids the join keys on; v2.test.claim.lexical_scope 29 PASS 0 FAIL. The earlier ordinal version (04e3221c) was also green; the join replaced it. The PARAMETER cell is closed at the identity join; the row stays open for its other named follow-ups (signature mentions that never reach a value frame; the classifier reading imports from a caller-supplied list). Rung for this cell is NOT raised beyond what those executed controls establish: a discriminating bound-CALL-before-free-call mispair control does not yet exist.",
  "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The sweep should count a site only where resolve itself would look the spelling up as a free name: a call-head (or pipe-target) reference that no lexical binder, module declaration or existing import answers, never a label. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the sweep's needed-row decision reads the same free-name classification resolve uses for the occurrence (v2.compiler.reference_site_collector's head binding, with labels excluded and binders honoured), proved by a roster control whose fixture is the specimen's shape -- a parameter and an argument label spelled like a row's call -- and which must come back Clean. Until then a sweep PR lists every module the generator touched where the spelling has no free call, and reverts it with a citation to this row.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-10-23 (sunny-bee-153, PR #14751, the OPPOSITE direction: a FALSE REFUSAL): the list_push sweep (roster_import_sweep_home_exit, home std.algebra, srv1 shards on the fixed sweep) refused dag/extdeps/npm.dag as home-name-locally-bound, yet that module has exactly three occurrences of list_push, all free calls through `|> list_push(..)` (no parameter, let, lambda parameter or match binder spelled list_push). The interim guard (roster_name_locally_bound over arrow_domain_binder_names, bind_binder, match_arm_candidate_names) therefore fires on a module with no binder: a real discriminating case for the guard repair. The line `import std.algebra { list_push }` was hand-applied (tidy-ant-251 no-veto, declared); the sweep re-run after the guard fix must reproduce it byte-identically, and that re-run is the oracle."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.reference_site_collector", decl_name: "site_head_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_role", decl_name: "reference_position_step", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.occurrence_identity", decl_name: "ReferencePosition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_site_is_free", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.module_acquisition", decl_name: "acquisition_head_is_candidate_module", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "the_called_parameter_head_at_the_call_is_bound_in_the_frame", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "a_parameter_is_not_bound_in_a_sibling_parameter_type", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.lexical_scope", decl_name: "a_type_annotation_sees_no_value_binder", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
